Package: mysterymodel
Title: Opinionated Workflow for Clinical Prediction Models
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("Tyler", "Muffly", email = "tyler.muffly@dhha.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An orchestration layer for clinical prediction modelling.
    Established engines do the statistics: 'rms' for regression, internal
    validation, calibration and nomograms, 'pmsampsize' for the sample size a
    model of a given shape requires, and 'pROC' for the interval on the
    c-statistic. This package supplies the workflow holding them together and
    the methodological safeguards that keep a published model honest:
    apparent, bootstrap-corrected and held-out performance are reported
    separately rather than interchangeably, a predictor that carries the
    outcome is refused, an interval states what it rests on or why there is
    none, and a nomogram must reproduce the model it was drawn from before it
    is returned. It makes no model-selection decision on the analyst's behalf
    and hides none.
